prompt:
A real photograph, taken with a good phone camera and looking exactly like a phone photograph, of the inside of a small neighbourhood laundrette in Berlin on a weekday afternoon, taken as a customer standing by the door a few metres away would take it, in a tall vertical picture, everything in sharp focus. Natural colours, white ceiling lights and grey daylight from the shop window on the right. The textures of real enamel, steel, glass, cotton, denim, wool, plastic, paper, tiles and skin, with the true depth and the slight lens perspective of a photograph.

The first reference picture shows the young woman in three-quarter view, the second from the front: her face, her dark blonde hair tied back in a ponytail, her build and her height stay exactly as in them. Use them for the person only; her clothes here are a grey hoodie, black leggings and white sneakers.

Every object stands on its own, with a little space around it, so that the eye can tell at once where each thing is. Nothing in the picture carries any writing, numbers or print: the washing machines have plain round doors and a single plain dial with no markings, the detergent is in a plain white bottle, the soap is a plain bar, the newspaper shows only grey illegible lines, the wall clock has a plain face and no numbers, and nothing carries a sign, a logo or a brand.

THE WASHING MACHINES stand in a row along the left wall, four white front-loading washing machines, seen from slightly to the side. The second machine from the front has its round door open.

THE YOUNG WOMAN of the reference pictures crouches on one knee in front of the open machine, seen whole from her head to her sneakers, and is caught in the middle of loading it: she pushes a blue shirt into the drum with one hand while her other hand holds a white towel. A red plastic laundry basket stands on the floor next to her, with a pair of blue jeans, a yellow T-shirt, a red dress and a few grey socks heaped in it. A plain white bottle of detergent and a plain bar of soap stand on top of the machine above her, and a few coins lie beside them.

THE MIDDLE of the picture:
- a long wooden table for folding, with a folded green sweater and a folded blue blanket lying on it, and an iron standing on the table at its end;
- a grey metal waste bin standing by the table.

THE RIGHT SIDE of the picture, by the shop window:
- a wooden bench along the wall under the window, where an old woman of about seventy-five with short white hair, in a purple cardigan, sits reading a folded newspaper, a cup of coffee beside her on the bench;
- a small girl of about six with two dark braids and a yellow jumper sits next to her on the bench, her feet swinging, holding a red mobile phone with a dark screen with both hands;
- a tall green plant in a pot in the corner;
- the shop window with the grey street outside and a bicycle leaning against a lamp post.

THE BACK WALL, from the left to the right:
- a round wall clock with a plain white face and no numbers;
- a wooden shelf with a few plain white bottles and a stack of white towels on it;
- a white radiator under the shelf;
- a mirror in a plain black frame;
- the glass door of the laundrette, closed, with a pale green wall beside it.
